---
layout: null
---
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9 http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9/sitemap.xsd" xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  {% for post in site.posts %}
    <url>
      <loc>{{ site.url }}{{ post.url }}</loc>
      {% if post.lastmod == null %}
        <lastmod>{{ post.date | date_to_xmlschema }}</lastmod>
      {% else %}
        <lastmod>{{ post.lastmod | date_to_xmlschema }}</lastmod>
      {% endif %}
      <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
      <priority>0.7</priority>
    </url>
  {% endfor %}
  {% for page in site.pages %}
    {% comment %}
      site.pages includes the machine files the plugins emit — robots.txt,
      feed.xml, this sitemap, and the stylesheet GitHub Pages injects from its
      default theme, which does not exist in a local build. A sitemap lists
      pages to index, not the files beside them, so allow only URLs that end
      in a slash or .html rather than blacklisting extensions one at a time.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% assign is_page = false %}
    {% if page.url == '/' or page.url contains '.html' %}{% assign is_page = true %}{% endif %}
    {% assign last_char = page.url | slice: -1 %}
    {% if last_char == '/' %}{% assign is_page = true %}{% endif %}
    {% comment %}
      The home page and the blog index list posts, so they change whenever a
      post is published. A hand-written lastmod on them went stale for years;
      take the newest post's date instead.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% assign page_lastmod = page.sitemap.lastmod %}
    {% if page.url == '/' or page.url contains '/blog/' %}{% assign page_lastmod = site.posts.first.date %}{% endif %}
    {% unless is_page == false or page.sitemap.exclude %}
    <url>
      <loc>{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}</loc>
      {% if page_lastmod == null %} <lastmod>2017-11-10T00:20:35+00:00</lastmod>
      {% else %} <lastmod>{{ page_lastmod | date_to_xmlschema }}</lastmod>
      {% endif %}
      {% if page.sitemap.changefreq == null %} <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
      {% else %} <changefreq>{{ page.sitemap.changefreq }}</changefreq>
      {% endif %}
      {% if page.sitemap.priority == null %} <priority>0.5</priority>
      {% else %} <priority>{{ page.sitemap.priority }}</priority>
      {% endif %}
     </url>
    {% endunless %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% comment %}
    The Ariana Project, Helios and the water simulator are each built and
    deployed from their own repository (AndrewKL/ArianaLinearAProject,
    AndrewKL/Helios3BodyProblemVisualizer, AndrewKL/NavierStokesSimulation)
    and served under this domain because the CNAME here claims it. Jekyll
    cannot see those pages, so list their entry points by hand; when one of
    those builds starts publishing its own sitemap, point robots.txt at it.
  {% endcomment %}
    <url>
      <loc>{{ site.url }}/ArianaLinearAProject/</loc>
      <lastmod>2026-09-24T00:00:00+00:00</lastmod>
      <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
      <priority>0.9</priority>
    </url>
    <url>
      <loc>{{ site.url }}/Helios3BodyProblemVisualizer/</loc>
      <lastmod>2026-09-25T00:00:00+00:00</lastmod>
      <changefreq>monthly</changefreq>
      <priority>0.8</priority>
    </url>
    <url>
      <loc>{{ site.url }}/NavierStokesSimulation/</loc>
      <lastmod>2026-09-25T00:00:00+00:00</lastmod>
      <changefreq>monthly</changefreq>
      <priority>0.8</priority>
    </url>
</urlset>
